    "sourceHash": "178ab8219f72081fde12feaaaeae049823c4577ad545823bdd23878b88e16d53",
    "body": "Last weekend, I took part in the NASA Space Apps challenge. With my team, we built a 3D map of Mars using real HiRISE and Curiosity data.\n\nThe idea: use drones to scout ahead of rovers and help make exploration faster, cheaper, and safer. Small terrain details can make a big difference on a Mars mission.\n\nWe didn’t sleep much, but the atmosphere made up for it, especially with my amazing teammates Luca Macie, Nicolas Rufino Pinto and Galsan \n\nThanks to the NASA Space Apps Challenge organizing team, especially Don Crowley, for making it happen!\n\nTry it here: nasa.nicolasrufino.com⁠",
    "photos": [
      "https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D5622AQGuLV429zl7Tg/feedshare-shrink_800/B56aH1gx4.H4Ag-/0/1795120374083?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=yHRC1U4hzSrMicJHiVRzLWa51qEguExiK8h6-55sChA"
    ],
